## Findings and mandatory host conditions

**SI01 — MEDIUM.** Legacy wallet and X composing transactions do not declare isolation. Under a database default REPEATABLE READ or SERIALIZABLE, the existing allowed empty-account merge fails STORAGE_CONTRACT even before any Participant mapping exists. Public adapter correctly fails closed; the legacy hosts do not enforce the dependency. New wallet-links off flag cannot contain this already wired legacy path.

Declare READ COMMITTED on the affected composing interactive transactions and verify both existing callers under higher DB defaults, OR enforce/test runtime/deployment default for all relevant connections before any rollout. Merely describing it is insufficient. Do not remove adapter SHOW verification or edit applied migration. Root assigned separate author/reviewer fix after finding; that later source is outside this reviewed candidate.

**SI02 — MEDIUM / deployment privilege condition.** Row guard does not fire for TRUNCATE. Reviewer-owned schema owner can TRUNCATE Participant CASCADE and erase mappings while User remains. Ordinary non-owner runtime role explicitly granted SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE provisions and reads, but direct mapping delete fails23000, parent delete23503, TRUNCATE and trigger ALTER42501. Owner bypass and application-role privilege gap are distinct: actual application role could be unsafe, and has not been inspected here.

Before rollout, prove runtime credentials are non-owner/non-superuser, cannot TRUNCATE relevant tables or alter/disable/drop protective objects, and separate migrator/administrative credentials. If runtime uses owner-level authority today, implement the role separation and verify it; documentation alone cannot enforce this. A separately reviewed forward TRUNCATE fence could narrow that path, but cannot protect against an authorized superuser removing it. No applied migration edits are authorized.

**SI03 — LOW.** Current module docs still say uncommitted and independent review absent; old WIP correctly preserves the historical uncommitted source but must not stand as final current-source acceptance. Current doc should link this separate review with its conditions. Explicitly document legacy default isolation and TRUNCATE/runtime-role boundary. Original proposal and author-side reports must remain historical, unedited.

Author records later candidate/report and these open conditions in current docs/checkpoint; retain original historical hashes and failures. Preserve full T00627 NOT VERIFIED.

Higher database defaults were tested by running the two unchanged allowed legacy wallet/X merge tests in new processes. REPEATABLE READ and SERIALIZABLE each produce two STORAGE_CONTRACT failures even with no mappings. Returning to READ COMMITTED passes both. This is actual legacy-path incompatibility, not a future flag-contained feature. See isolation-probes.py, isolation-probe-results.json and the three JUnit files.

Role proof is bounded: reviewer-created non-owner ordinary-DML role can provision/read and rejects mapping deletion23000, parent deletion23503, TRUNCATE/ALTER42501. Schema owner TRUNCATE CASCADE removes mapping without row trigger; the reviewer intentionally rolls back and confirms restoration. Actual application credentials were not inspected, so their privilege safety remains NOT VERIFIED. A role/configuration fix is necessary if they retain these powers; documentation alone cannot make the invariant hold.

